Build the linux-dmabuf client-buffer plugin and give it dma-buf feedback.

- The compositor's dma-buf client buffer configure test links EGL::EGL, which
  nothing in qtwayland finds since the Wayland client moved to qtbase (6.10), so
  the plugin was silently never built.
- The plugin spoke protocol version 3 only. Mesa 25+ has no
  EGL_WL_bind_wayland_display (wl_drm), so its clients find the GPU only through
  dma-buf feedback (version 4): offer it when the DRM device behind the EGL
  display is known, with a sealed format table (implicit modifiers included).
  The protocol XML comes from wayland-protocols; qtbase bundles version 3.
- The global is created only once buffer import is set up.

QindaXR selects the plugin with QT_WAYLAND_HARDWARE_INTEGRATION; other
compositors keep wayland-egl unless they ask for it.

